---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Nav from '../../components/Nav.astro';
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Rig Equipment — Rig Types, Drill String, BOP Explained"
  description="Complete reference for oil rig equipment: rig types, the drill string, blowout preventers, and every major mechanical system on a rig."
  breadcrumbs={[{ label: 'Equipment', href: '/equipment' }]}
  lang="en"
  alternateHref="/es/equipment"
>
  <Nav slot="nav" lang="en" alternateHref="/es/equipment" />
  <Footer slot="footer" lang="en" />

  <div class="page-hero">
    <div class="page-hero-eyebrow">02 — Equipment</div>
    <h1>Rig <span>Equipment</span></h1>
    <p class="page-hero-sub">Every core mechanical system on a drilling rig, from the rig itself down to the bit thousands of feet below.</p>
  </div>

  <section class="block">
    <h2 class="sr-only">Equipment guides</h2>
    <div class="card-grid">
      <div class="card">
        <span class="card-icon">🏗️</span>
        <h3>Types of Drilling Rigs</h3>
        <p>Land rigs, jack-ups, semi-submersibles, drillships, platforms, and barges compared with specs and day rates.</p>
        <a href="/equipment/rig-types" class="card-link">Read More →</a>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <span class="card-icon">🔩</span>
        <h3>The Drill String</h3>
        <p>Every component from top drive to bit — drill pipe, collars, BHA, MWD tools, and bit types.</p>
        <a href="/equipment/drill-string" class="card-link">Read More →</a>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <span class="card-icon">🔒</span>
        <h3>Blowout Preventers</h3>
        <p>How a BOP stack seals the well — annular preventers, rams, pressure ratings, and testing requirements.</p>
        <a href="/equipment/bop" class="card-link">BOP Types &amp; Stack →</a>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <span class="card-icon">🧯</span>
        <h3>Accumulator Function Test &amp; Drill</h3>
        <p>Initial pressure, per-component open/close timing against API STD 53, recharge time, and drill report sections.</p>
        <a href="/equipment/accumulator" class="card-link">Read More →</a>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <span class="card-icon">🔧</span>
        <h3>Bridge Plug</h3>
        <p>Drillable vs. retrievable, wireline vs. mechanical setting, pressure/temp ratings, failure modes, and how it differs from a cement retainer — with an interactive 3D model.</p>
        <a href="/equipment/bridge-plug" class="card-link">Read More →</a>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <span class="card-icon">✂️</span>
        <h3>Casing Cutter</h3>
        <p>Mechanical vs. chemical cutting, running and actuation, generic ratings, failure modes, and how it differs from a section mill — with an interactive 3D model.</p>
        <a href="/equipment/casing-cutter" class="card-link">Read More →</a>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <span class="card-icon">⚙️</span>
        <h3>Section Mill</h3>
        <p>Single-trip vs. two-trip mills, swarf handling, generic ratings, failure modes, and how it differs from a casing cutter — with an interactive 3D model.</p>
        <a href="/equipment/section-mill" class="card-link">Read More →</a>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <span class="card-icon">🪟</span>
        <h3>Window Mill</h3>
        <p>The starting/window/taper mill sequence, whipstock setting and orientation, failure modes, and how it differs from a section mill — with an interactive 3D model.</p>
        <a href="/equipment/window-mill" class="card-link">Read More →</a>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <span class="card-icon">🔓</span>
        <h3>Safety Joint</h3>
        <p>Mechanical vs. hydraulic release designs, where it's placed in a fishing or liner string, and common failure modes — with an interactive 3D model.</p>
        <a href="/equipment/safety-joint" class="card-link">Read More →</a>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <span class="card-icon">📡</span>
        <h3>MWD Tool</h3>
        <p>Mud pulse telemetry, MWD vs. LWD, where it sits in the BHA, and common failure modes — with an interactive 3D model.</p>
        <a href="/equipment/mwd-tool" class="card-link">Read More →</a>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <span class="card-icon">🧷</span>
        <h3>Packer</h3>
        <p>Permanent vs. retrievable, the polished bore receptacle, and how it differs from a bridge plug — with an interactive 3D model.</p>
        <a href="/equipment/packer" class="card-link">Read More →</a>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <span class="card-icon">📐</span>
        <h3>Whipstock</h3>
        <p>How its concave face deflects a window mill into the casing wall, the pilot lug, and orientation before milling — with an interactive 3D model.</p>
        <a href="/equipment/whipstock" class="card-link">Read More →</a>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <span class="card-icon">🔗</span>
        <h3>Liner Hanger</h3>
        <p>Why a liner runs instead of full casing, how the slips carry its weight, and the liner top packer — with an interactive 3D model.</p>
        <a href="/equipment/liner-hanger" class="card-link">Read More →</a>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <span class="card-icon">🚰</span>
        <h3>Cement Retainer</h3>
        <p>How the pump-through valve works during a squeeze job, drillable vs. retrievable, and how it differs from a bridge plug — with an interactive 3D model.</p>
        <a href="/equipment/cement-retainer" class="card-link">Read More →</a>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <span class="card-icon">⬇️</span>
        <h3>Float Sub</h3>
        <p>How its flapper or ball-and-seat check valve stops backflow, and how it differs from a float shoe or collar — with an interactive 3D model.</p>
        <a href="/equipment/float-sub" class="card-link">Read More →</a>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <span class="card-icon">🔀</span>
        <h3>Crossover Sub</h3>
        <p>Joining different thread types and diameters in a string, the tapered-shoulder failure point, and how it differs from a bit sub — with an interactive 3D model.</p>
        <a href="/equipment/crossover-sub" class="card-link">Read More →</a>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <span class="card-icon">🌀</span>
        <h3>Under-Reamer</h3>
        <p>Folding arms that pass a restriction closed then cut hole wider once extended, hydraulic vs. mechanical actuation, failure modes, and how it differs from a hole opener — with an interactive 3D model.</p>
        <a href="/equipment/under-reamer" class="card-link">Read More →</a>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <span class="card-icon">🎯</span>
        <h3>Stabilizer</h3>
        <p>String vs. near-bit vs. roller-reamer placement, straight vs. spiral blade design, failure modes, and how it differs from an under-reamer — with an interactive 3D model.</p>
        <a href="/equipment/stabilizer" class="card-link">Read More →</a>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <span class="card-icon">🔃</span>
        <h3>Reversing Tool</h3>
        <p>How reverse circulation carries junk and debris back up the string, port actuation, failure modes, and how it differs from a float sub — with an interactive 3D model.</p>
        <a href="/equipment/reversing-tool" class="card-link">Read More →</a>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <span class="card-icon">🔨</span>
        <h3>Hydraulic Jar</h3>
        <p>Up jar vs. down jar, how a jar accelerator stores extra energy, failure modes, and how it differs from a safety joint — with an interactive 3D model.</p>
        <a href="/equipment/hydraulic-jar" class="card-link">Read More →</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="block">
    <div class="section-eyebrow">Core Systems</div>
    <h2 class="section-title">Every Rig's <span>Six Systems</span></h2>
    <div class="card-grid grid-2">
      <div class="card">
        <span class="card-icon">🏗️</span>
        <h3 style="font-size:14px;">Hoisting System</h3>
        <p>Derrick, crown block, travelling block, and drawworks raise and lower the drill string.</p>
        <a href="/equipment/hoisting-system" class="card-link">Read More →</a>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <span class="card-icon">🔄</span>
        <h3 style="font-size:14px;">Rotating System</h3>
        <p>Top drive or rotary table turns the drill string and bit at controlled RPM.</p>
        <a href="/equipment/rotating-system" class="card-link">Read More →</a>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <span class="card-icon">💧</span>
        <h3 style="font-size:14px;">Fluid Circulation</h3>
        <p>Mud pumps force drilling fluid down-hole. Returns carry cuttings to surface shakers.</p>
        <a href="/equipment/fluid-circulation-system" class="card-link">Read More →</a>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <span class="card-icon">🔒</span>
        <h3 style="font-size:14px;">Pressure Control</h3>
        <p>Blowout preventers (BOPs) seal the wellbore during kicks and emergencies.</p>
        <a href="/equipment/bop" class="card-link">Read More →</a>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <span class="card-icon">⚡</span>
        <h3 style="font-size:14px;">Power Generation</h3>
        <p>Diesel generators or SCR systems supply the massive electrical loads of rig equipment.</p>
        <a href="/equipment/power-generation-system" class="card-link">Read More →</a>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <span class="card-icon">🛢️</span>
        <h3 style="font-size:14px;">Mud Pit System</h3>
        <p>Shale shakers, desanders, desilters, and degassers process returned drilling fluid.</p>
        <a href="/equipment/mud-pit-system" class="card-link">Read More →</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
